   "abbr": [],
   "means": "parents (the father and mother together); 'parentum' is 'of the parents'",
   "events": "all",
   "role": "person",
   "note": "The word list gives 'parentes' (and 'genitores'); 'parentum', 'parentibus' and 'parens' are the same word with other endings. In baptisms you will often meet 'ex legitimis parentibus', 'of lawful (married) parents'. It does not name them: look for 'patre' and 'matre', or for the names beside it. 'Nomina parentum' is a common column heading: the names of the parents.",
   "src": [
    "fswiki"
   ]
  },
  {
